                <td>₹11,800</td>
            </tr>

        </table>

        <hr>

        <h2>GST Tax Structure in India</h2>

        GST is divided into three main components.

        <h3>CGST – Central GST</h3>
        <p>Collected by the Central Government.</p>

        <h3>SGST – State GST</h3>
        <p>Collected by the State Government.</p>

        <h3>IGST – Integrated GST</h3>
        <p>Applied on interstate transactions.</p>

        <hr>

        <h2>Intra-State vs Inter-State GST Example</h2>

        <h3>Same State Transaction</h3>

        <p>Product value: ₹10,000</p>

        <ul>
            <li>CGST 9% = ₹900</li>
            <li>SGST 9% = ₹900</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Total = ₹11,800</p>

        <h3>Different State Transaction</h3>

        <ul>
            <li>IGST 18% = ₹1,800</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Total = ₹11,800</p>

